  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1215 AM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nFor Friday into the upcoming weekend, the models generally agree in \nshowing some remnant mid-level weakness remaining over the \nnorthwestern Gulf, with weak ridging building in from the west. Any \nrain chances should be confined to the coastal plains region, with \ndry weather expected elsewhere. Models indicate a slight increase in \n850mb temperatures and this may translate into a degree or two \nupward nudge in temperatures across the region. We will continue to \nmonitor for the possibility of maximum temperatures and peak heat \nindex values near Heat Advisory criteria for areas generally along \nand east of Interstate 35 for the upcoming weekend. \n\nFor early next week, mid and upper level high pressure builds over \nthe southeastern U.S. allowing for a deeper south to southeasterly \nflow in the lower and mid-levels of the atmosphere to develop. No \nsignificant change in temperatures are anticipated with both high \nand low temperatures likely to remain above climatological normals. \nSome low rain chances will likely persist over the coastal plains, \nwith dry weather expected elsewhere.",
